# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# D-93 with A3, under --walk-methods: unit_make_adder_model_call.lm2's text, the first call before the
# model's definition (as the refused fixture had it).  The host is walked; its call of the model is a CALL over
# the model's occurrence with n as a hidden input -- q 6, r 16, n 22, add(1) = 23.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    int: q (addN: 1)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    n: n + 10
    int: r (addN: 1)
    n: q + r
    return: addN

@: add makeAdder(5)
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 23
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
